  "decision": "NO_CHANGE",
  "workflow_yaml": null,
  "rationale": "The workflow is a minimal reusable workflow that only calls the GitHub API via actions/github-script to check if a commit is from a merged PR. It has no dependency installation, build steps, test matrix, or long-running operations. The job typically completes in seconds. None of the evidence-supported optimizations apply: there are no dependencies to cache (P-LIT-GHA-CACHE, P-LIT-CONFIG-REUSE), no matrix to fail-fast (P-LIT-FAIL-FAST), and no history of runaway execution that would justify a custom timeout (P-LIT-CUSTOM-TIMEOUT). The experimental evidence for timeouts involves workflows with npm ci, lint, typecheck, and other multi-step processes — not a single API-call step. Adding a timeout or other changes would be unnecessary and unsupported.",
  "evidence_ids": []
}
